From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:08:52 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] kcm_networkmanagement_qml: status line, labelled
 Add/Configure, NetworkManager reads after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same changes as kcm_networkmanagement (10d7b53) for the QML variant, so both look and read alike.
Page type: List (connections) + editor; connection settings, handler and editor unchanged.

Moved / renamed (ui/main.qml):
- Status line first: PlasmaNM.NetworkStatus activeConnections or 'Not connected', created by a Loader 50 ms after open.
- 'Add new connection' (icon-only, bottom) -> 'Add Connection…' labelled button beside the search field;
  'Configure' (icon-only) -> 'Configure…' labelled. Forget and Export keep icons, now with Accessible.name.
- Empty editor side shows 'Select a connection to see and change its settings.'
- No inventory rows exist for this KCM id (it shares the rows of kcm_networkmanagement), so no markers beyond comments.

Speed (from code, kcm.cpp constructor): before the first frame it ran NetworkManager::networkInterfaces() (blocking
GetDevices + per-device properties), primaryConnection()/listConnections() with a sort over all connections, and
onSelectedConnectionChanged(), which loads the whole editor for the preselected connection. All of that now runs in
startDeferredWork(), 100 ms after construction (single-shot; skipped when a connection is already selected, e.g. by launch
argument or click). useApMode (read by nothing in QML; Handler computes its own) now has a NOTIFY signal.
Not changed: KcmIdentityModel / creatable models still built with main.qml. After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-017, HIG-019, HIG-020.

Not built yet. Uncertain: 100 ms is a guess for 'after the first frame' (no afterRendering hook in KQuickConfigModule
checked); anchors of search field vs Add button; NetworkStatus import in this module.

